<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Callao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Combate del Dos de Mayo · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chincha-islands-war">Chincha Islands War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/callao">Callao</a> was fought on 2 May 1866 between a Spanish naval squadron under Casto Méndez Núñez and the coastal fortifications of Callao, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>'s main port, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chincha-islands-war">Chincha Islands War</a>. After a day-long bombardment both sides claimed victory, but the Spanish fleet soon withdrew from the Pacific. The battle is celebrated in Peru as the Combate del Dos de Mayo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-callao.jpg" alt="Battle of Callao" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CombateDosdeMayo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
